{"name":"Tonic","hex":"#deddaa","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tonic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to tension, especially of the muscles.","Restorative; curative; or invigorating."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A substance with medicinal properties intended to restore or invigorate.","Tonic water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tonic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tonic water","blocks":[{"text":"Tonic water is a carbonated soft drink in which quinine is dissolved. Originally used as a prophylactic against malaria, modern tonic water typically has a significantly lower quinine content and is often more sweetened than the original medicinal form. It is consumed for its distinctive bitter flavour."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Tonic_water_uv.jpg/330px-Tonic_water_uv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tonic_water"},{"title":"Tonic (music)","blocks":[{"text":"In music, \"tonic\" refers to the originating note or chord of a particular key."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tonic_(music)"},{"title":"Tonic (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Tonic is an American rock band, formed in 1993 by Emerson Hart and Jeff Russo. Later members have included Dan Lavery, Kevin Shepard, Pierce Bowers and Dan Rothchild. The band signed with Polydor Records in 1995, through which they released their debut studio album Lemon Parade (1996). Despite lukewarm critical and commercial response, it spawned the singles \"Open Up Your Eyes\" and \"If You Could Only See\" in 1997, which significantly entered several  Billboard charts, including Adult Alternative Airplay, Radio Songs, Alternative Airplay and Mainstream Rock. The album received platinum certification by the Recording Industry Association of America (RIAA)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Tonic_07_06_2016_-2_%2828210309935%29.jpg/330px-Tonic_07_06_2016_-2_%2828210309935%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tonic_(band)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Tonic_water_uv.jpg/500px-Tonic_water_uv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Tonic_water_uv.jpg/500px-Tonic_water_uv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Under ultraviolet light, the quinine in tonic water fluoresces, as seen with this bottle of Canada Dry tonic water.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATonic_water_uv.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Gin_Tonic_4.jpg/500px-Gin_Tonic_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Gin_Tonic_4.jpg/1280px-Gin_Tonic_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Gin_Tonic_4.jpg/500px-Gin_Tonic_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gin and tonic","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGin_Tonic_4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Tequila_%26_Tonic.jpg/500px-Tequila_%26_Tonic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Tequila_%26_Tonic.jpg/1280px-Tequila_%26_Tonic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Tequila_%26_Tonic.jpg/500px-Tequila_%26_Tonic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tequila and tonic cocktail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATequ